    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d74-a2">

                <pb facs="0209" n="113" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg113"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure B in No. 53.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Saturday</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-07-06"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 6,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>We regret to say that the United States minister, the Hon. J. P. Root, is
                    suffering from an attack of small-pox, contracted during his indefatigable
                    efforts to combat that fell complaint while acting in his self-imposed capacity
                    as a member of the board of health, in Santiago. We learn from a private source
                    that the attack from which Mr. Root is suffering is of a mild form, and we are,
                    therefore, glad to say there is no ground for alarm. The illness of the
                    honorable gentleman has elicited the sympathy <pb facs="0210" n="114"
                        xml:id="pg114"/> of the entire population of the capital, as it will most
                    assuredly do from all our readers, both far and wide, who are already acquainted
                    with the eminent and disinterested services he has rendered to suffering
                    humanity during the prevalence of the present epidemic in the-capital.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
